  "problem": "Let $C$ be the boundary of the top (tilted) surface of our solid. The curve $C$ is oriented counter-clockwise when viewed from above, as shown in the diagram. Use Stokes' theorem to write down the integral that gives the circulation of the air along $C.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The required circulation is ${\u222e}_{C}^{}F\\cdot dr\\,={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$",
